2026-11-07T07:06:56.8460990Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8490570Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8492520Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8494210Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8494520Z 
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8494980Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8495320Z 
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8495660Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8496210Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8496470Z 
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8496720Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8497070Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8497290Z 
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8497510Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T07:06:56.8497910Z   $ sh ./install-nix
